{
  "id": "deployment_rollout_stuck",
  "type": "troubleshooting",
  "question": "What fields in DeploymentSpec control the rolling update strategy, and how does DeploymentStatus expose rollout progress and health via conditions?",
  "resource": "io.k8s.api.apps.v1.Deployment",
  "scope": "Namespaced",
  "multi_hop": true,
  "ground_truth": {
    "answer": "The strategy field in DeploymentSpec is a DeploymentStrategy with a type (RollingUpdate or Recreate). When type is RollingUpdate, the rollingUpdate field (a RollingUpdateDeployment) defines maxUnavailable (maximum number of Pods that can be unavailable during update) and maxSurge (maximum number of Pods that can be created above the desired count). The progressDeadlineSeconds field sets the timeout in seconds before a stalled rollout is declared failed. Rollout health is reflected in the status field (a DeploymentStatus) which contains conditions (a list of DeploymentCondition with type, status, reason, and message), as well as updatedReplicas and unavailableReplicas counters for tracking progress.",
    "context": [
      "io.k8s.api.apps.v1.DeploymentStrategy: type is RollingUpdate or Recreate; rollingUpdate field is a RollingUpdateDeployment",
      "io.k8s.api.apps.v1.RollingUpdateDeployment: maxUnavailable and maxSurge control the rolling update pace and pod availability during update",
      "io.k8s.api.apps.v1.DeploymentStatus: conditions is a list of DeploymentCondition; updatedReplicas and unavailableReplicas track rollout progress",
      "io.k8s.api.apps.v1.DeploymentCondition: type (Available, Progressing), status, and reason fields indicate rollout state and health"
    ],
